      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im getting this annoying SettingWithCopyWarning in my notebook. i'm trying to filter a df and then add a new column to that slice but it keeps popping up. can u explain why this happens and how i should actually do it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This warning occurs because pandas often makes a copy of the DataFrame when performing operations to retain the original immutability (e.g., slicing). The proper way to avoid this issue is to chain your operations onto the original DataFrame (df) instead of creating intermediate copies. \n\nIn your case, you can chain the filter and assignment as follows: `df[condition].copy()`, replacing `condition` with your filtering conditions. This way, the original DataFrame remains unchanged, and you'll avoid the warning. \n\nExample:\n```python\ndf = df[df['column'] = 'value']  # Filter\ndf['new_column'] = new_value  # Add a new column to the filtered data.\n```",
      "source": "target",
